# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit .env.local -- this repo is public.
#
# Variable NAMES only. A value in this file is a leaked credential, and the
# .gitignore that protects .env.local deliberately does not protect this one.

# Narration. Both pitch modes render TTS by default: a gauge render on every
# script draft, and the ship take. See claude/skills/pitch/SKILL.md Step 4b.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Which voice narrates. render.py also takes --voice; without either it stops
# rather than guessing. List what your account has:
#   python3 claude/skills/pitch/scripts/render.py --list-voices
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=

# Slide generation. Replicate is the priced line -- FLUX is quotable per image,
# which is what lets an ask be itemized. See the Leonardo pricing scan for why
# a subscription-priced provider cannot appear as a per-round cost.
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=

# Optional, and not the priced line. Leonardo bills GPU-load tokens against a
# subscription with no published per-model table.
LEONARDO_API_KEY=

# Deck layout and visual design. Pro tier or above; the API exports PNG
# directly, so slides drop straight into assemble.py. On paid plans credits
# burn only on API calls -- a 14-card illustrated deck is ~40-250 of Pro's
# 4,000/month, so the subscription is the cost and the per-round marginal is
# noise. Being a subscription, it is disclosed as a fixed monthly line and
# never divided into a per-round ask figure.
GAMMA_API_KEY=
